// Two instances of one generic type are two types (`Result<Unit, IoError>` is not `Result<isize, IoError>`), and
// nothing converts between them. Through 0.9.618 the class identity rule stopped at "same template" — meant for the
// smart-pointer upcast `Shared<Square>` into `Shared<Shape>` — so this reached clang ("assigning to
// 'kama__Result_kama__Unit…' from incompatible type") while `kama check` called the file clean. The same in an
// assignment, an argument and a return, and for `Optional<int64>` from an `Optional<int32>`.
import { std::io::IoError };

fn Result<isize, IoError> count() { return Result::Ok(value: 1); }

fn uint8 main() {
    Result<Unit, IoError> r = count();   // -> REJECT
    return 0;
}
